The Authority is undertaking preliminary market engagement in relation to the potential future supply and through-life support of Fixed and Portable Atmosphere Monitoring Systems (AMS) and associated equipment and services.
The potential requirement may include, but is not limited to:
- supply of AMS equipment, approved replacements, spares, consumables, accessories and associated support equipment;
- inspection, maintenance, calibration, survey, repair and refurbishment of in-scope equipment;
- technical support, fault investigation, defect resolution and reliability improvement;
- logistics, inventory and supply-chain support;
- technical documentation and configuration management;
- software and firmware support;
- obsolescence management, including identification and implementation of suitable replacement solutions;
- training and associated support;
- mobilisation, transition and knowledge transfer; and
- performance management and reporting.
The purpose of this market engagement is to help the Authority understand market capability, capacity and appetite, and to obtain information that may assist in developing the requirement and informing the future procurement and commercial strategy.
The scope, procurement route, commercial model, contract structure, duration, estimated value and delivery arrangements have not yet been determined and may be subject to change. Any subsequent procurement opportunity will be advertised separately through the appropriate procurement notice.
This notice is published for preliminary market engagement and information-gathering purposes only. It does not constitute a call for competition, invitation to tender, pre-qualification exercise, request for expressions of interest, offer or commitment by the Ministry of Defence to undertake a procurement or place a contract.
Interested organisations should refer to the Atmosphere Monitoring Systems Request for Information (RFI) for further information and instructions on how to participate in the market engagement. - https://contracts.mod.uk/esop/guest/go/opportunity/detail?opportunityId=61704

To support the development of the next phase of regulations, Employment and Social Development Canada (ESDC) is launching this RFI to gather information from digital technology vendors and suppliers on their current accessibility-related capabilities, practices, implementation challenges, and readiness with respect to artificial intelligence (AI) systems, software, and hardware.
The RFI seeks information on:
•	Current accessibility capabilities, policies, and practices relating to software, hardware, and AI systems;
•	Conformance with relevant accessibility standards and specifications for software, hardware, and AI systems;
•	Approaches to incorporating accessibility throughout the product lifecycle, including design, development, testing, deployment, and procurement;
•	Barriers, implementation challenges, and considerations associated with achieving accessibility; and,
•	Organizational readiness to meet potential future accessibility requirements.
The information collected through this process will help inform the development of the next phase of Digital Technologies Accessibility Regulations under the ACA.
